            "tagline": "The body is just meat that hasn't been told what it could be yet.",
            "role": "Bio-artificer / Mutator",
            "pillar": "Flesh-mancy",
            "terms": [
                [
                    "Vitae",
                    "Blood, tissue, and stolen vigor rendered down into usable current. Tracked as a daily pool, refreshed through grim ritual — drawing your own blood, harvesting a corpse, milking a captive."
                ],
                [
                    "The Cut",
                    "Opening flesh — yours or someone else's — and working Vitae into it to prepare a Graft. Your version of \"infuse.\""
                ],
                [
                    "Bloom",
                    "What happens when a Cut goes wrong: tissue overgrows, mutates, or rebels outright — the same radiation-soured biology that grows raging spirits and worse out in the Glasslands, just closer to home. Roll on the Bloom Table (§4)."
                ],
                [
                    "Graft",
                    "Your consumable creations — serums, boil-sacs, bile lances, wet ammunition. Replaces the standard alchemical item list."
                ],
                [
                    "Stock",
                    "Your working specialty as a fleshmancer. Functions as your subclass, chosen at 1st level."
                ]
